.TH expr_eval 3 2026-10-23 "Graph Drawer expr man-pages 1.0.13"
.SH NAME
expr_eval \- expression evaluator
.SH LIBRARY
Graph Drawer Expression Evaluator Library
.RI ( libexpr ,\~ \-lexpr )
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.BR #include\~"expr.h"
.P
.BI "double expr_eval(const struct expr *" ep ",double " input ");"
.BI "double expr_vevalx(const struct expr *" ep ",va_list " ap ");"
.BI "double expr_evalx(const struct expr *" ep "," ... ");"
.BI "double expr_eval1(const struct expr *" ep ");"
.BI "[[removed]] int expr_step(const struct expr *" ep " ,expr_t " input ",expr_t *restrict " output ",struct expr_inst **restrict " saveip ");"
.BI "expr_t expr_eval_callback(const struct expr *" ep ",expr_t " input ",const struct expr_eval_callback *" ec ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.BR expr_eval()
function evaluates the
.B struct expr
object
.I ep
with the argument
.IR input ,
corresponding to the
.I asym
argument in
.BR expr_new()
and
.BR expr_init() .
.P
The
.BR expr_vevalx() , expr_evalx()
functions behave like
.BR expr_eval()
but fetch arguments from
.IR ap , ... .
.P
The
.BR expr_eval1()
function is equivalent to
.RI expr_eval( ep ,0.0).
.P
The
.BR expr_step()
function evaluates the
.B struct expr
object
.I ep
step-by-step, the
.I *saveip
must be set to
.I ep->data
at the start.
.P
The
.BR expr_eval_callback()
function evaluates the
.B struct expr
object
.I ep
and run the callback function at the begin and end of each instruments.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The
.BR expr_eval() , expr_eval_callback()
returns the result of the evaluation.
.P
The
.BR expr_step()
returns 1 if completed and write the result to
.I *output
or 0 if not completed.
.SH WARNING
The
.BR expr_vevalx() , expr_evalx()
are not safe when the source of expression is untrusted, even with the
.B EXPR_IPROTECT
flag. In the case, a string in the from "
.IR asym -->x0; asym -->x1;...;undef( asym );
" must be patched at the head of the expression to limit the number of arguments. Or the
.I argc
field in
.I extarg
must be set to the count of arguments(<=255).
.SH ATTRIBUTES
.TS
allbox;
lbx lb lb
l l l.
Interface	Attribute	Value
